═══ R8 EN reply complete (collagen/vegetarian) — guard: clean ═══
Q: I have spondylosis and osteoporosis and my doctor requires me to take collagen as part of treatment. But I have been a vegetarian for 14 years. Can I take normal collagen?
Sources: Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) | Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: qa_metaphysics,qa_general,introduction
  ✓ substantial reply (>600 chars)
  ✓ ends cleanly (punctuation/emoji, not mid-word)
  ✓ answers the vegetarian-collagen question
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Fourteen years of vegetarian practice — that's a beautiful foundation, and I understand the conflict you're feeling right now. 🙏

Master Lu addressed this exact situation in *Buddhism Q&A*:

> When you consume any medicine or health supplements that contain ingredients such as gelatine or fish oil, if your body does not reject the taste, then perhaps you have not reached the level where you are completely observing your precepts. However, it would still be best to avoid consuming such products as they contain animal by-products.

So Master Lu's guidance leans toward **avoiding animal-derived collagen where possible**, but he is not harsh about it. What he emphasises most is your **intention** — whether you are seeking it out for enjoyment, or taking it reluctantly because of a genuine medical need.

A few practical steps:

**1. Ask your doctor about alternatives first.**
There are plant-based options and nutrients that support collagen formation — vitamin C, soy protein, calcium, and other supplements. Master Lu strongly recommended soy products for vegetarians because they're high in protein. Ask your doctor whether these can meet your treatment needs. If a genuine vegetarian option exists, take that.

**2. If your doctor says there is truly no substitute:**
Master Lu's way in "no choice" situations is to speak to Guan Yin Bodhisattva in your heart before taking it — something simple and sincere, such as:

*"Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva, please forgive me, [your full name]. I am taking this only because of my illness and my doctor's instruction. I do not wish to break my vegetarian practice."*

Keep looking for a plant-based replacement in the meantime. Reluctance and repentance are very different from indulgence.

**3. Treat body and spirit together.**
Master Lu always taught us to cooperate fully with doctors — Buddhism clears the spiritual obstacles, medicine treats the physical body. Both hands together. Please don't stop your treatment.

Alongside your treatment, reciting the **Great Compassion Mantra** is the sutra for health and energy, and praying:

*"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me, [your full name], with good health and heal my spine and bones."*

May I ask — are you already doing a daily recitation practice? If you tell me where you're at, I can suggest a practice that suits your situation properly rather than guessing. 🙏

All Guan Yin Citta materials are free of charge. Scripture resources: https://xlfm.my/jingwen
Chanting guide videos: https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

